  "slug": "chromosome-inactivation-detecting-dna-f070",
  "summary": "Single-cell atlases now pair snATAC and scRNA with chromatin topology to link regulatory elements, GWAS variants and cell-type-specific gene expression.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is cell-type-resolved measurement of regulatory chromatin. The RPE and choroid atlas integrates scRNA and snATAC across 102 donors aged 0 to 99 years, linking AMD GWAS variants to LIPG and COL4A3. The 9p21 study uses single-cell tools to deconvolve p16INK4A, p14ARF and p15INK4B transcripts and maps cis-regulatory elements, with chromatin topology and distal elements underlying divergent cell-type-specific regulation of cell cycle genes. What is new is joint readout of accessibility with expression and 3D organization within a shared cell-type framework. The lung atlas, which defines 142 cell types across more than 18M cells, and the laying hen liver single-nucleus atlas address cell-type resolution without this chromatin focus, and the PFAS hepatotoxicity analysis uses public RNA-seq rather than single-cell data.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-30"
}
